# What must not end up in the image.
#
# The Dockerfile copies named directories rather than `.`, so most of this is
# belt and braces — except for `data/`, which it does copy. A local SQLite
# ledger baked into an image is the specific accident worth preventing: the
# container would start with somebody's real fills in it, and on a host with no
# writable disk it would look like a working village that never updates. That
# failure has its own message in src/deploy.py, and it should stay theoretical.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.env
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# The ledger, in every form.
data/*.db
data/*.db-journal
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
data/notifications.log
data/metrics.json

# Written at runtime, never shipped.
vault/
logs/
run/
dashboard/
uploads/
processed/

# Tests and docs do not need to be in a running container.
tests/
*.md
!README.md
